# Test-First Discipline

**Activation:** `alwaysApply: false` — when triggers in `agent-discipline-core.mdc` match, **Read this file before editing**. Triggered rules are mandatory, not optional.

Treat every non-trivial monitor change as test-first work.

**Hard requirement:** Any work that fixes a discovered defect or failure must also add or extend a regression test per **`every-error-regression-test.mdc`** (that rule takes precedence on “no test, no done”).

## Required workflow

- Before changing behavior, add or update the smallest relevant test in `HPCPerfStats/monitor/tests/` that captures the intended behavior or reproduces the bug.
- Prefer seeing that test fail first for bug fixes and behavior changes; then implement code changes and make it pass.
- For refactors, lock existing behavior with tests before simplifying/moving code.
- If a true test-first sequence is blocked (for example missing configured build tree), document the blocker in the task and add regression coverage immediately after code changes.

## Scope expectations

- Apply this to monitor C sources, `configure.ac`, emit/schema shape, and packaging tied to behavior.
- Select the narrowest test level that proves correctness first (unit/contract in `tests/test_*.c`); escalate per **`global-testing-discipline.mdc`**.
- **New C functions** require tests per **`monitor-c-new-function-unittests.mdc`**.
- Do not mark work complete without running the relevant tests for touched behavior.

## Pre-merge verification matrix (monitor)

| Change touches | Minimum run |
|----------------|-------------|
| Pure helper / parser in `src/` | Targeted `tests/test_*.c` via `make check` |
| Substantive monitor C / Autotools | **`build_static_bundle.sh`** + **`make check`** on **arches that compile the change** |
| Portable / multi-arch (shared code, **DCGM GPU**) | Also **`cross_compile_test.sh --force-foreign --fail-fast`** |
| x86-only LIKWID uncore / RAPL / CPUID | x86_64 only; **skip aarch64** |
| Shared LIKWID adapters / overlay / both-arch bundle | **x86_64 and aarch64** |
| DCGM **CPU** only | aarch64 only; **skip x86_64** |
| `hpcperfstats.spec` / version | **`rpmspec -P`**; optional full RPM prep |
| After successful verify | **`make distclean`** in build dir per **`monitor-post-verify-distclean.mdc`** |

## Integration with implementation workflow

- **`implementation-review-workflow.mdc`** — pre-code planning and post-code self-review; regression coverage and test runs are part of the post-implementation review.
- **`monitor-c-testing-standards.mdc`** — pyramid, fixtures, contract tests.
- **`monitor-dual-verify-cross-and-static.mdc`** — static bundle on required arches; foreign cross only for portable / multi-arch diffs.
